        "original_id": "a2302b9f-f143-58d6-92fa-f6cefe839c45",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James Hill; John Vereker, 6th Viscount Gort\n- Roles: British Army officer; Field Marshal\n- Events: Battle of France; evacuation of Dunkirk\n- Places: Brussels; De Panne\n\nFacts:\n- John Vereker, 6th Viscount Gort, was born on 10 July 1886 and died on 31 March 1946.\n- John Vereker, 6th Viscount Gort, was a senior British Army officer and held the rank of Field Marshal.\n- In May 1940, during the Battle of France, James Hill was attached to the command post of Field Marshal Lord Gort after briefly commanding a platoon.\n- In May 1940, during the evacuation of Dunkirk, James Hill oversaw the evacuation of Brussels and the beach at De Panne while serving at Field Marshal Lord Gort’s command post.",
